and expanded again. secondPhasePreProcess() then compares the expanded entries pairwise, so a short malicious glob can cause excessive CPU and memory consumption during pattern compilation. This issue is fixed in version 11.0.1.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","metrics":{"baseScore":6.9},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-118764","epss":0.00409,"percentile":0.35655,"date":"2026-11-24"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-118764","cwe":"CWE-405","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"minimatch","version":"10.2.6"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-g3hv-75wg-m249","versionConstraint":">=7.0.0,<11.0.1 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"11.0.1"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/minimatch@10.2.6?package-id=852193e3bb25b937","name":"minimatch","version":"10.2.6","type":"npm","locations":[{"path":"/examples/library-lending/web-nextjs/pnpm-lock.yaml","accessPath":""}],"language":"javascript","licenses":[],"cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:minimatch_project:minimatch:10.2.6:*:*:*:*:node.js:*:*"],"purl":"pkg:npm/minimatch@10.2.6","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-rhh4-g77r-r9qj","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-rhh4-g77r-r9qj","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/vercel/next.js/security/advisories/GHSA-rhh4-g77r-r9qj","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119349","https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/6596840a0fa3c2633735b05e41ca3d9ab01ece41","https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases/tag/v16.4.5","https://nextjs.org/blog/november-2026-security-release"],"description":"Next.js: Cross-user cache disclosure and poisoning in Next.js use cache with binary arguments","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","metrics":{"baseScore":6.3},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-119349","epss":0.00391,"percentile":0.33718,"date":"2026-11-24"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-119349","cwe":"CWE-694","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary"}],"fix":{"versions":["16.4.5"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"16.4.5","date":"2026-11-20","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.220915},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-119349","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119349","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/6596840a0fa3c2633735b05e41ca3d9ab01ece41","https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases/tag/v16.4.5","https://github.com/vercel/next.js/security/advisories/GHSA-rhh4-g77r-r9qj","https://nextjs.org/blog/november-2026-security-release"],"description":"Next.js is a React framework for building full-stack web applications. From 16.0.0 until 16.4.5, Next.js App Router applications that pass binary arguments, such as Uint8Array or Blob values, to functions using the 'use cache' directive can generate identical cache keys for distinct arguments. Requests with different binary arguments can therefore share a cached result, causing cross-user disclosure of cached data or allowing one request to poison results returned to another user. This issue is fixed in version 16.4.5.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","metrics":{"baseScore":6.3},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-119349","epss":0.00391,"percentile":0.33718,"date":"2026-11-24"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-119349","cwe":"CWE-694","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Primary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"javascript","namespace":"github:language:javascript","package":{"name":"next","version":"16.4.1"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-rhh4-g77r-r9qj","versionConstraint":">=16.0.0,<=16.4.4 (semantic)"},"fix":{"suggestedVersion":"16.4.5"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:npm/next@16.4.1?package-id=0337ccfbbb37b149","name":"next","version":"16.4.1","type":"npm","locations":[{"path":"/examples/library-lending/web-nextjs/pnpm-lock.yaml","accessPath":""}],"language":"javascript","licenses":[],"cpes":["cpe:2.3:a:vercel:next.js:16.4.1:*:*:*:*:node.js:*:*"],"purl":"pkg:npm/next@16.4.1","upstreams":[]}},{"vulnerability":{"id":"GHSA-mfr8-8qww-v76h","dataSource":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-mfr8-8qww-v76h","namespace":"github:language:javascript","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/vercel/next.js/security/advisories/GHSA-mfr8-8qww-v76h","https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/d605874e5a4b8b6b7dca1b6e07bcabb44d0e2e5b","https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases/tag/v16.4.5","https://nextjs.org/blog/november-2026-security-release"],"description":"Next.js: Information disclosure across root params when a 'use cache' function is called through unstable_cache()","cvss":[{"type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N","metrics":{"baseScore":6.3},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-119790","epss":0.00362,"percentile":0.30402,"date":"2026-11-24"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-119790","cwe":"CWE-362","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}],"fix":{"versions":["16.4.5"],"state":"fixed","available":[{"version":"16.4.5","date":"2026-11-17","kind":"first-observed"}]},"advisories":[],"risk":0.20453},"relatedVulnerabilities":[{"id":"CVE-2026-119790","dataSource":"https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-119790","namespace":"nvd:cpe","severity":"Medium","urls":["https://github.com/vercel/next.js/commit/d605874e5a4b8b6b7dca1b6e07bcabb44d0e2e5b","https://github.com/vercel/next.js/releases/tag/v16.4.5","https://github.com/vercel/next.js/security/advisories/GHSA-mfr8-8qww-v76h","https://nextjs.org/blog/november-2026-security-release"],"description":"Next.js is a React framework for building full-stack web applications. From 16.3.0 until 16.4.5, Next.js applications using the same 'use cache' function directly during rendering and through unstable_cache() can disclose cached data across root params when that function reads a root param. During the first fill after a cold process start, cross-request deduplication allows a concurrent unstable_cache() request to join the direct call's in-flight fill and receive its result before the root param mismatch is rejected. unstable_cache() then persists that result under a key that omits root params, causing later requests for other root param values to receive the same entry until revalidation or eviction. Exploitation requires the unstable_cache() request to arrive while the first fill is in flight. Outside this race, nesting 'use cache' inside unstable_cache() raises an unsupported-operation error, and avoiding that nesting prevents the issue. This issue is fixed in version 16.4.5.","cvss":[{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"4.0","vector":"CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:X/CR:X/IR:X/AR:X/MAV:X/MAC:X/MAT:X/MPR:X/MUI:X/MVC:X/MVI:X/MVA:X/MSC:X/MSI:X/MSA:X/S:X/AU:X/R:X/V:X/RE:X/U:X","metrics":{"baseScore":6.3},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-119790","epss":0.00362,"percentile":0.30402,"date":"2026-11-24"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-119790","cwe":"CWE-362","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"javascript-matcher","searchedBy":